// @run
// @log 31
// @log 32
// @log 33
// @log 34
// @log 1
// @log 35
// @warning Unused parameter `t`
// @warning Unused parameter `t`
// @warning Unused parameter `t`
// @warning Unused parameter `t`
// @warning Unused parameter `p`
// THE UNUSED PARAMETERS ARE DECLARED, NOT DELETED. Each `t` is what makes its callee GENERIC,
// and `srch`'s `p` is what makes that callee CLONEABLE with an empty `fnTyParams` — the shape
// whose mark master drops silently. Removing either removes the case.
// CONTRACT (must-RUN): D926. Both `??` owner marks are ARENA-NODE keyed — `anonLeafParamMoved`
// by `Param` index, `anonLeafRetMoved` by `FuncDecl` index — and `monoMakeInstance` mints new
// `Param` and `FuncDecl` nodes for every instance. `collectAnonShapes` is pass 3 and
// `monomorphize` is pass 16, so the marks are final at clone time and are then silently
// dropped: every reader (`emitOneFuncType`, `emitFuncCode`, `paramStructIdxOf`,
// `anonLeafRetRowOf`) resolves through the POST-mono declaration.
//
// THE TWO SITES HAD DRIFTED TO OPPOSITE WRONG ANSWERS ABOUT IT. `anonLeafParamArgsOk` refused a
// callee with `fnTyParams` OUTRIGHT; `anonLeafMarkRetMoved` had no guard at all. The refusal was
// neither necessary nor sufficient for its own stated reason: `monoIsGenericDecl` clones for an
// UN-ANNOTATED parameter too, so `function src(p: {r: i32}, t)` has an empty `fnTyParams`, is
// marked, is cloned, and is CHECK-CLEAN INVALID WASM on master — as is a GENERIC callee that
// returns a literal, which no guard covered. Both are filed
// (`distilled/named/d926_hole_param_clone`, `d926_generic_ret_clone`) and both run here.
//
// CARRYING THE MARK NEEDS NO GUARD, and that is what makes deleting the refusal safe rather
// than merely narrower. `anonLeafSupersedeOf` is a bounds-checked identity outside the family,
// so an instance whose parameter annotation was RE-SYNTHESISED per pin (the `p: T` case the old
// comment was actually right about) resolves to a row the merge never touched and the redirect
// is a no-op. Only a parameter whose pinned row IS the family's narrow row moves — and for a
// concrete annotation the arena type node is literally shared with the original.
//
// `distilled/named/d926_generic_unrelated` is the control: a generic function ELSEWHERE in a
// module with a merged family runs on master and here alike, so it is the callee being cloned
// and not the monomorphizer's presence.

// ---- a GENERIC callee whose parameter is returned ----
function srcg<T>(p: { r: i32 }, t: T): { r: i32 } | null { p }

function rg() {
  const g1 = srcg({ r: 31 }, 1) ?? { r: "s" }
  print(g1.r)
}
rg() // 31

// ---- TWO instances of one template, each carrying the mark ----
function srct<T>(p: { r: i32 }, t: T): { r: i32 } | null { p }

function rt() {
  const g1 = srct({ r: 32 }, 1) ?? { r: "s" }
  print(g1.r)
  const g2 = srct({ r: 33 }, "a") ?? { r: "s" }
  print(g2.r)
}
rt() // 32, 33

// ---- a generic callee returning a LITERAL: the RETURN mark, which had no guard at all ----
function srcl<T>(t: T): { r: i32 } | null { { r: 34 } }

function rl() {
  const g1 = srcl(1) ?? { r: "s" }
  print(g1.r)
}
rl() // 34

// ---- and the UN-ANNOTATED parameter, which mono clones with no `fnTyParams` to refuse on ----
function srch(p: { r: i32 }, t) { t }

function srcp(p: { r: i32 }, t): { r: i32 } | null { p }

function rp() {
  print(srch({ r: 0 }, 1))
  const g1 = srcp({ r: 35 }, 1) ?? { r: "s" }
  print(g1.r)
}
rp() // 1, 35
